# 6. FIRESTORE DATA MODEL

Do NOT copy PostgreSQL blindly into Firestore.

Design Firestore around the application.

Preferred model:

```text
users/{uid}
    email
    familyName
    displayName
    emailVerified
    accountStatus
    createdAt
    updatedAt
    legacyUserId
```

Family trees:

```text
trees/{treeId}
    ownerUid
    name
    createdAt
    updatedAt
```

People:

```text
trees/{treeId}/persons/{personId}
    firstName
    middleName
    lastName
    maidenName
    gender
    birthDate
    deathDate
    birthPlace
    deathPlace
    notes
    photoPath
    legacyPersonId
    createdAt
    updatedAt
```

Relationships:

```text
trees/{treeId}/relationships/{relationshipId}
    person1Id
    person2Id
    type
    status
    label
    startDate
    endDate
    legacyRelationshipId
    createdAt
    updatedAt
```

If the actual application supports shared trees, add an appropriate membership model such as:

```text
trees/{treeId}/members/{uid}
```

with:

```text
role
joinedAt
```

Do not implement shared ownership unless the real application requires it.

