# 51. FINAL SUCCESS CRITERIA

The migration is complete only when:

```text
Firebase Hosting serves the frontend
Firebase Authentication handles users
Firestore stores application data
Storage stores application-owned uploads
Firebase Functions handles privileged backend operations
Firebase Security Rules protect user data
family tree CRUD works
relationship graph works
authentication works
cross-user access is blocked
production no longer calls Render
production no longer requires PostgreSQL
DATABASE_URL is unnecessary
Render PostgreSQL is unnecessary
Cloud Run lineage API is unnecessary
blank-page behavior is fixed
```

Historical data recovery is reported independently.

An unavailable historical database must NOT prevent creating the Firebase-native application.

However, never fabricate historical records.

